<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thracian Tomb of Kazanlak</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 300 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> · Also known as Kazanlak Tomb</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Thracian Tomb of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazanlak">Kazanlak</a> is a beehive-shaped brick tomb near Kazanlak in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>, discovered in 1944 and dated to around 300 BCE. Its corridor and burial chamber are decorated with well-preserved wall paintings of a funeral feast, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariot</a> race and Thracian warriors, among the finest surviving Hellenistic paintings. It was inscribed as a World Heritage Site in 1979.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kazanlak-tomb.jpg" alt="Thracian Tomb of Kazanlak" width="320" height="304" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kmrakmra · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kazanluk_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
